# The build stage copies the whole repo and then builds one workspace. Anything
# here is either rebuilt inside the image, irrelevant to it, or must never enter
# it in the first place.
#
# Note the `**/` — a bare `node_modules` matches only the one at the root, and
# this is a monorepo where every workspace can have its own.

# Installed in the deps stage, for the image's own platform. A node_modules
# built on a developer's machine carries the wrong native binaries — sharp above
# all — and the failure surfaces as a crash at the first upload.
**/node_modules

# Build output. The image builds its own.
**/.next
**/out
**/build
**/coverage
**/*.tsbuildinfo
**/next-env.d.ts

# Secrets. Belt and braces: these are gitignored too, but a build context is
# read from the working tree rather than from git, so an untracked .env would
# otherwise be copied straight into a layer.
**/.env
**/.env.*

# Not the CMS's business.
.git
.github
.claude
.agents
.vercel
docs
design
*.md

# Local noise.
**/.DS_Store
**/npm-debug.log*
